From df88c948426a5741262ca04e021c4c3c5eeff36a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dolf3131 <144650661+dolf3131@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:19:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] lone stream: launch the MTP absorb before the verify's commit
 (TF_ABSORB_FIRST, default on) + TF_ROUND_PROFILE

The absorb reads none of what commit writes (its own cache, length, position and buffers; commit writes the
DeltaNet states, conv windows, n-gram history and pos), so commit's host work (a replay launch per DeltaNet layer
when a draft is rejected) now runs while the absorb is on the GPU; decode_ahead.start still follows commit (it
reads the new n-gram history). Same kernels on the same data on one stream: tests/cuda/test_flashnext_L7.py and
test_flashnext_decode_ahead_cuda.py give the same results with TF_ABSORB_FIRST=1 and =0 (and as TF-tc).

TF_ROUND_PROFILE=1 prints, every TF_ROUND_PROFILE_EVERY lone rounds, the host ms per round between fixed marks
(events after each replay), so the stretches the GPU waits for the host can be split. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
